{"path":"s31","heading":"Form and contents of arbitral award.","in_1996":true,"nodes_1996":[{"path":"s31","node_type":"section","number":"31","heading":"Form and contents of arbitral award.","text":""},{"path":"s31.ss1","node_type":"subsection","number":"1","heading":null,"text":"An arbitral award shall be made in writing and shall be signed by the members of the arbitral tribunal."},{"path":"s31.ss2","node_type":"subsection","number":"2","heading":null,"text":"For the purposes of sub-section (1), in arbitral proceedings with more than one arbitrator, the signatures of the majority of all the members of the arbitral tribunal shall be sufficient so long as the reason for any omitted signature is stated."},{"path":"s31.ss3","node_type":"subsection","number":"3","heading":null,"text":"The arbitral award shall state the reasons upon which it is based, unless—"},{"path":"s31.ss3.cl(a)","node_type":"clause","number":"a","heading":null,"text":"the parties have agreed that no reasons are to be given, or"},{"path":"s31.ss3.cl(b)","node_type":"clause","number":"b","heading":null,"text":"the award is an arbitral award on agreed terms under section 30."},{"path":"s31.ss4","node_type":"subsection","number":"4","heading":null,"text":"The arbitral award shall state its date and the place of arbitration as determined in accordance with section 20 and the award shall be deemed to have been made at that place."},{"path":"s31.ss5","node_type":"subsection","number":"5","heading":null,"text":"After the arbitral award is made, a signed copy shall be delivered to each party."},{"path":"s31.ss6","node_type":"subsection","number":"6","heading":null,"text":"The arbitral tribunal may, at any time during the arbitral proceedings, make an interim arbitral award on any matter with respect to which it may make a final arbitral award."},{"path":"s31.ss7","node_type":"subsection","number":"7","heading":null,"text":""},{"path":"s31.ss7.cl(a)","node_type":"clause","number":"a","heading":null,"text":"Unless otherwise agreed by the parties, where and in so far as an arbitral award is for the payment of money, the arbitral tribunal may include in the sum for which the award is made interest, at such rate as it deems reasonable, on the whole or any part of the money, for the whole or any part of the period between the date on which the cause of action arose and the date on which the award is made."},{"path":"s31.ss7.cl(b)","node_type":"clause","number":"b","heading":null,"text":"A sum directed to be paid by an arbitral award shall, unless the award otherwise directs, carry interest at the rate of eighteen per centum per annum from the date of the award to the date of payment."},{"path":"s31.ss8","node_type":"subsection","number":"8","heading":null,"text":"Unless otherwise agreed by the parties,—"},{"path":"s31.ss8.cl(a)","node_type":"clause","number":"a","heading":null,"text":"the costs of an arbitration shall be fixed by the arbitral tribunal;"},{"path":"s31.ss8.cl(b)","node_type":"clause","number":"b","heading":null,"text":"the arbitral tribunal shall specify—"},{"path":"s31.ss8.cl(b).sc(i)","node_type":"subclause","number":"i","heading":null,"text":"the party entitled to costs,"},{"path":"s31.ss8.cl(b).sc(ii)","node_type":"subclause","number":"ii","heading":null,"text":"the party who shall pay the costs,"},{"path":"s31.ss8.cl(b).sc(iii)","node_type":"subclause","number":"iii","heading":null,"text":"the amount of costs or method of determining that amount, and"},{"path":"s31.ss8.cl(b).sc(iv)","node_type":"subclause","number":"iv","heading":null,"text":"the manner in which the costs shall be paid."},{"path":"s31.ss8.expl1","node_type":"explanation","number":"1","heading":null,"text":"For the purpose of clause (a), \"costs\" means reasonable costs relating to—"},{"path":"s31.ss8.expl1.sc(i)","node_type":"subclause","number":"i","heading":null,"text":"the fees and expenses of the arbitrators and witnesses,"},{"path":"s31.ss8.expl1.sc(ii)","node_type":"subclause","number":"ii","heading":null,"text":"legal fees and expenses,"},{"path":"s31.ss8.expl1.sc(iii)","node_type":"subclause","number":"iii","heading":null,"text":"any administration fees of the institution supervising the arbitration, and"},{"path":"s31.ss8.expl1.sc(iv)","node_type":"subclause","number":"iv","heading":null,"text":"any other expenses incurred in connection with the arbitral proceedings and the arbitral award."}],"events":[{"instrument":"3/2016","title":"Arbitration and Conciliation (Amendment) Act, 2015 (No. 3 of 2016)","effective":"from 23 Oct 2015 (Ordinance 9 of 2015)","edges":[{"instrument":"3/2016","old":"s31.ss7.cl(b)","new":"s31.ss7.cl(b)","op_type":"substitute","source":"rule","group":"3/2016|s16.cl(i)","confidence":1.0,"rationale":null},{"instrument":"3/2016","old":"s31.ss8","new":"s31.ss8","op_type":"substitute","source":"rule","group":"3/2016|s16.cl(ii)","confidence":1.0,"rationale":null}],"instructions":{"3/2016|s16.cl(i)":"in sub-section (7), for clause (b), the following clause shall be substituted, namely:— ‘(b) A sum directed to be paid by an arbitral award shall, unless the award otherwise directs, carry interest at the rate of two per cent. higher than the current rate of interest prevalent on the date of award, from the date of award to the date of payment. Explanation.—The expression “current rate of interest” shall have the same meaning [[margin: 14 of 1978.]] as assigned to it under clause (b) of section 2 of the Interest Act, 1978.’;","3/2016|s16.cl(ii)":"for sub-section (8), the following sub-section shall be substituted, namely:— “(8) The costs of an arbitration shall be fixed by the arbitral tribunal in accordance with section 31A.”."},"intent":[{"unit":"3/2016|s16","status":"sourced","claim":"The amendment is intended to ensure that the default rate of interest reflects prevailing commercial realities instead of an arbitrary 18% rate.","tier":"report","quote":"[NOTE: Explanation 1 ensures that the default rate of interest is in line with\nprevailing commercial realities and not an arbitrary figure of 18%.","document_id":59,"span":[119711,119857],"attribution":{"by":"Law Commission of India, Report No. 246","role":"committee","where":"Law Commission of India, Report No. 246: Amendments to the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996 (August 2014), part 1"},"tiers_searched":["sor","debate","report"]}]}]}